                    %li
                      %a{:href => "#ReferencesEllipticGeneraAsPartitionFunctionsOfEStrings"} E-string elliptic genus
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em partition function
            is a certain assignment that may be extracted from a system in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+mechanics"} statistical mechanics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %p
            If the quantum field theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            is presented as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            on a category of
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} tori
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of the values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(T)
            assigned to these by the QFT.
          %p
            By the axioms of functoriality and symmetric monoidalness of a QFT, this means that the partition function is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            over the value of the QFT in the cylinder obtained by cutting the torus open.
          %p
            This is where the partition function originally derives its name from: typically for QFTs on
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            the value of the QFT on a cylinder of
            %em length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi t
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(- t H)
            for some operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          %h2#origin_of_the_term Origin of the term
          %p
            When one thinks of the QFT — under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotation
            — as describing a physical system in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+mechanics"} statistical mechanics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            acts on is the vector space of all states of the system and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is the operator whose eigenstates are the states of definite energy. The expression
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi t
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tr(exp(-t H))
          %p then is interpreted as
          %blockquote
            %p
              sum over all states
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
              of the system and weigh each one by its energy
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi Ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\Psi
          %p
            This involves, conversely, counting for each fixed energy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi Ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\Psi
            the number of states of that energy. This will typically be a sum over certain partitions of various particles of an ensemble into various “bins” of partial energies. Therefore the term
            %em partition
            function.
          %p
            In fact, the common letter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            used to denote QFTs (or at least
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            %em Zustandssumme
            — from German
            %em Zustand
            for “state” .
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mellin+transform"} Mellin transform
            of the partition function is known in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            as the
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+parameter"} Schwinger parameter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline+theory"} worldline theory
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+regularization"} zeta regulated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Partition function for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
          %p
            Partition function for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
          %p
            Partition function for the
            = succeed ":" do
